c309-6a71-4c92-9e7e-cf23182224f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "b4743f4f-4d5a-44b3-ba19-f8d98770a6fe", "type": "concept", "title": "intrinsic value"}, {"id": "43c17b0c-2c4b-458f-9dd3-a81f6be6032a", "type": "concept", "title": "instrumental value"}, {"id": "6d81aaab-2fd1-4429-9354-940ee803c1d4", "type": "concept", "title": "well-being"}, {"id": "5977daea-4be3-42ac-9abb-0e723cfafb21", "type": "concept", "title": "reason for action"}, {"id": "83f922af-32bf-4eb6-a88b-cd058935f2cf", "type": "concept", "title": "desire"}, {"id": "fc5800e7-3d2f-4c17-b8d6-736245beb5bd", "type": "concept", "title": "moral motivation"}, {"id": "e300072f-860d-4d1a-af99-820a789e4523", "type": "concept", "title": "internalism"}, {"id": "4e428c1f-4d64-4617-a6ec-e4fea2e722c1", "type": "concept", "title": "externalism"}, {"id": "6f42ec1b-7d3d-4adc-bc4e-bbfc4bf5cbef", "type": "concept", "title": "egoism"}, {"id": "00868c8a-3685-459d-ad22-61be0011c938", "type": "concept", "title": "altruism"}], "description": "Students ask why anything matters and how moral judgments motivate action."}]}, {"id": "a83777e1-180d-435f-8e25-4cfb452dd17e", "type": "topic", "title": "Consequentialism and Utilitarian Moral Reasoning", "description": "Consequentialist theories evaluate actions by their outcomes. Students examine the appeal and limits of utility, welfare, aggregation, and impartiality.", "children": [{"id": "0bb5e2d1-5149-4b66-b343-504479c7c6d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classical utilitarianism", "children": [{"id": "1cc2a09b-2aa3-4a02-b7cd-afe4d73836f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "0c64d40c-9d66-4d39-b84a-de8814075a33", "type": "concept", "title": "utility"}, {"id": "d5294e23-42ea-4d37-9aa7-892019f7823d", "type": "concept", "title": "pleasure"}, {"id": "2ac047f3-aef1-4ce7-aba1-36a3d9ca70c4", "type": "concept", "title": "pain"}, {"id": "572ba37e-e73a-4e1f-abab-c705f6c899d5", "type": "concept", "title": "happiness"}, {"id": "b83