ation"}], "description": "Students see why ethical judgment is not only rule application."}, {"id": "9110ebdc-d124-4607-9f0d-c66134a166c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moral psychology and responsibility", "children": [{"id": "a58e4316-9a30-4765-a2d4-e905b2e6d6cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "87ad70d3-00de-420f-b29b-3da2b2ae5cd4", "type": "concept", "title": "responsibility"}, {"id": "30186597-5e06-47e0-ab0b-85b08d01d28d", "type": "concept", "title": "blame"}, {"id": "dcb8fe7f-f19a-436b-a125-bd5033dda4d7", "type": "concept", "title": "praise"}, {"id": "2eab3692-3169-43f1-b193-cc9e11ea53b4", "type": "concept", "title": "excuse"}, {"id": "e9dd211d-ee63-4bc3-ab50-6806db7c968c", "type": "concept", "title": "intention"}, {"id": "2f77bf7d-c050-4dea-96a8-4364fd830809", "type": "concept", "title": "weakness of will"}, {"id": "c826e7be-1baf-44b2-a268-bd27dba57753", "type": "concept", "title": "habit formation"}, {"id": "237ec7f0-b911-4d1b-a3a8-5c9c503ad8b9", "type": "concept", "title": "situationism"}, {"id": "e4ba6401-5ffc-4191-9282-2a3a1ac5c9b9", "type": "concept", "title": "character trait"}, {"id": "8f82ac4f-fb66-4bd7-aa07-19c474ee890b", "type": "concept", "title": "moral luck"}], "description": "Students connect character to agency, blame, praise, and self-formation."}]}, {"id": "e720b4ad-285f-420d-b4b7-15abc722f68d", "type": "topic", "title": "Natural Law, Care Ethics, Feminist Ethics, and Non-Western Moral Traditions", "description": "This unit broadens the ethical map. Students compare frameworks that foreground nature, relationship, dependency, oppression, harmony, community, and spiritual discipline.", "children": [{"id": "76bc606d-58f7-4c65-b767-07c3a1f1b689", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Natural law and rights traditions", "children": [{"id": "1d753ec4-fef8-43df-8002-ab9fc340d2f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "a07dbe3a-9bae-451e-86ca-e22a5c9a86ee", "type": "concept", "title": "natural