-be01-762209d656ea", "type": "concept", "title": "begging the question"}, {"id": "1a4ba466-7f7e-42f0-ba1f-f4b803206a24", "type": "concept", "title": "equivocation"}, {"id": "2d479b0a-f091-4b27-b1d7-ba16dec73b91", "type": "concept", "title": "slippery slope"}, {"id": "2905eaca-6b2c-4fb2-9874-a5d8df87ed0d", "type": "concept", "title": "hasty generalization"}, {"id": "89a90b34-7140-43a6-a637-45630a391c16", "type": "concept", "title": "appeal to authority"}, {"id": "ac9ceec4-f8bc-4297-9d14-296ed839c8fc", "type": "concept", "title": "red herring"}, {"id": "df1b837e-d64f-4f5e-bf65-37abfb031044", "type": "concept", "title": "post hoc fallacy"}], "description": "Students learn common mistakes without using fallacy labels as shortcuts for analysis."}]}, {"id": "a0b2f063-3678-4864-95d5-f06e275988b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Conceptual Analysis, Definitions, and Philosophical Method", "description": "This unit shows how philosophers sharpen unclear ideas. Students learn to define concepts, test borderline cases, and explain why distinctions matter.", "children": [{"id": "85d64923-8443-4218-9d61-e18a2eb11f92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Definitions and necessary conditions", "children": [{"id": "6fefc46b-f04c-4656-b57e-c5d58d1e1c6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "7b3ad2aa-4c78-45ce-aa45-d01b449b1590", "type": "concept", "title": "necessary condition"}, {"id": "4011152c-9aa5-4091-9e4f-fceb59581d84", "type": "concept", "title": "sufficient condition"}, {"id": "704fb9d8-03b7-4fae-8c38-b053cc2bcc9f", "type": "concept", "title": "jointly sufficient"}, {"id": "0eaa167a-51b0-49b4-a831-5d0cb06c3591", "type": "concept", "title": "counterexample"}, {"id": "db6b021b-11d5-4104-a214-74cff61852d6", "type": "concept", "title": "genus and differentia"}, {"id": "ce3aaa48-acb4-4bac-976c-6ca253f42ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "stipulative definition"}, {"id": "aa3ad8bd-b0c2-4f6d-bc27-3a3041974b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "lexical definition"}, {