"title": "reductio ad absurdum"}, {"id": "907d3cf2-5812-4841-8822-3de3ceccf196", "type": "concept", "title": "dilemma"}, {"id": "e4384dab-cfcf-49fd-97a7-c09fdd99aa28", "type": "concept", "title": "analogy"}, {"id": "1efd6f8a-73bc-4d03-9ac7-f520d2661a6a", "type": "concept", "title": "reflective equilibrium"}, {"id": "84e03b7b-af5c-47a9-b264-5211456a88e7", "type": "concept", "title": "conceptual analysis"}, {"id": "2deb8be3-b9a5-4806-b6d3-3998f32e7866", "type": "concept", "title": "phenomenological description"}, {"id": "4792dca8-ba7d-4ec3-ba6c-cdd587134665", "type": "concept", "title": "genealogy"}, {"id": "09823f9e-01a0-4868-ab21-508efe3607ef", "type": "concept", "title": "hermeneutics"}, {"id": "c7b3bb83-9cba-4f84-9cf2-d919e02e6fac", "type": "concept", "title": "pragmatic test"}], "description": "Students learn common moves in philosophical reasoning and debate."}]}, {"id": "c0ed66d3-f4a0-498f-9c6d-7fc677b40f52", "type": "topic", "title": "Metaphysics: Reality, Identity, Causation, and Free Will", "description": "Metaphysics asks what the world is like at its most basic level. Students investigate existence, change, personal identity, causation, and whether human action is free.", "children": [{"id": "a43beb0a-e847-40f7-8b2c-44f3d7689518", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Being, substance, and reality", "children": [{"id": "1d1791c7-929b-4692-972e-f79bc29c6408", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "33024c99-2146-4962-84b4-e86b8c4d4e60", "type": "concept", "title": "ontology"}, {"id": "4650bd8a-f0ac-4229-a4c0-138976873cc8", "type": "concept", "title": "substance"}, {"id": "1e7ac52c-0b83-41a2-84a7-772d6fd52304", "type": "concept", "title": "property"}, {"id": "0603eb2f-96eb-4661-b886-8680991e5168", "type": "concept", "title": "universal"}, {"id": "1a8233bd-451a-4c3e-8fec-da1410b3d582", "type": "concept", "title": "particular"}, {"id": "11727cad-a298-43d5-845d-b197ffeae7ee", "type": "concept", "title": "materialism"}, {"id": "11303f33-be05-41fd-9368-0f1e1c1f3818", "type": "concept", "title": "idealism"}, {"id": "f96d5ee7-3b84-4243-91b5-283d005ea618", "type": "concept", "title": "dualism"}, {"id": "07b4237a-ac38-498c-9ed0-e3ea189a532e", "type": "concept", "title": "monism"}, {"id": "afb877e4-4cf5-4100-8fb2-bf88ad47aba7", "type": "concept", "title": "realism"}], "description": "Students explore competing accounts of what fundamentally exists."}, {"id": "c6db185d-74a6-4514-b8e7-6d42d60553e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Identity and persistence", "children": [{"id": "e2a3c39f-1fc6-4c22-9149-8a7da53fa396", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "f8c5713a-fa30-43fb-a790-3ee9cc38774c", "type": "concept", "title": "identity over time"}, {"id": "9a4e7f49-c368-4c1c-a1ef-df734c9f0b2a", "type": "concept", "title": "qualitative identity"}, {"id": "34ad1fa2-09da-4ffe-bd72-efe3f7cbe697", "type": "concept", "title": "numerical identity"}, {"id": "ef705655-942f-47b8-b5e0-18d47e393ade", "type": "concept", "title": "Ship of Theseus"}, {"id": "f54c5b18-e7e8-44ea-9a37-ee6a99a6ddf2", "type": "concept", "title": "personal identity"}, {"id": "6804f4c1-b074-4a6a-addb-8dfab4dd65a3", "type": "concept", "title": "memory criterion"}, {"id": "f6bba712-eb28-4a23-acfd-9bde4734406b", "type": "concept", "title": "bodily criterion"}, {"id": "620b9acc-0f76-41dc-acef-dc0584035ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "psychological continuity"}, {"id": "ea463a27-0201-4b80-8b9b-cc434a25a4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "animalism"}, {"id": "a75bbe82-6fe9-4a0c-b862-f28ab7c74ab8", "type": "concept", "title": "fission case"}], "description": "Students ask what makes a thing or person the same over time."}, {"id": "2ebbc339-97cd-4a13-bbcc-007e9c187b69", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causation and freedom", "children": [{"id": "3b023e5e-5836-4d45-a6bb-afa4916a809c", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "4afbd7ba-b228-43e0-bfed-3cc284522997", "type": "concept", "title": "cause"}, {"id": "f5f244ac-dfa8-42f4-9ea1-0be4f4254afe", "type": "concept", "title": "necessary condition"}, {"id": "b69ea0db-e61a-4b5f-8d91-9719bf5ba77a", "type": "concept", "title": "sufficient condition"}, {"id": "00edf12f-36a3-41c7-8b49-201e394eaed7", "type": "concept", "title": "determinism"}, {"id": "dfae0c6f-9f67-4479-8a9d-1b7263e23046", "type": "concept", "title": "libertarian free will"}, {"id": "0c5d711d-05ec-41da-8905-339d5e15dfcf", "type": "concept", "title": "compatibilism"}, {"id": "d54e1e91-1239-4029-ae8f-585995713ba2", "type": "concept", "title": "hard determinism"}, {"id": "3181ad50-4b4a-480e-8330-bff9494fd445", "type": "concept", "title": "agency"}, {"id": "a9653b7c-c0db-4dea-8cdd-48b2c6eb681b", "type": "concept", "title": "moral responsibility"}, {"id": "69ff5449-e286-4009-97f0-ef4dc46ff5ec", "type": "concept", "title": "alternative possibilities"}], "description": "Students analyze whether causal order leaves room for responsibility."}]}, {"id": "02b1e421-d589-4d06-9de6-fef24888d9b0", "type": "topic", "title": "Epistemology: Knowledge, Skepticism, Evidence, and Testimony", "description": "Epistemology asks what knowledge is and how beliefs become justified. Students learn to evaluate evidence, testimony, perception, and skeptical challenges.", "children": [{"id": "18d8950f-1150-4300-934d-f8ae91489f97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Knowledge and justification", "children": [{"id": "f14c4fd9-f0be-4e56-9525-20ef464a5838", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "9df34e3a-8101-4a4d-b2c0-0ffd0d46e3b6", "type": "concept", "title": "belief"}, {"id": "7014db77-b0e2-4499-a565-f405ed1d02b9", "type": "concept", "title": "truth"}, {"id": "3799e4c1-c09d-430a-bf6b-d860a8cec0e8", "type": "concept", "title": "justification"}, {"id": "a24db3b2-972c-474e-8c98-c41de064f60e", "type": "concept", "title": "justified true belief"}, {"id": "b47eecd8-e7cd-4d05-9129-7a74dccba673", "type": "concept", "title": "Gettier case"}, {"id": "39a3db61-4b2f-4e9a-b34d-d360968756e2", "type": "concept", "title": "reliabilism"}, {"id": "0ac24fcf-665d-4590-927f-4d4b22ec9c0b", "type": "concept", "title": "foundationalism"}, {"id": "bcd4647e-1f0a-44d5-96cd-36223d9a65db", "type": "concept", "title": "coherentism"}, {"id": "c66c5c9f-2c8a-4bd5-8ec6-8d411a24c5dd", "type": "concept", "title": "internalism"}, {"id": "71d3f074-8523-4795-8f0d-c82ebd4cf50d", "type": "concept", "title": "externalism"}], "description": "Students examine classic and contemporary accounts of knowledge."}, {"id": "dea4f179-cec5-4211-a7e5-caab6c04a9d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Skepticism and doubt", "children": [{"id": "477e5b08-c12f-4cf7-9e6d-d4fbd764dc54", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "ae84ab43-1818-4183-828a-61669522c954", "type": "concept", "title": "methodic doubt"}, {"id": "81335f91-eec2-493a-a287-7e3aa64b5349", "type": "concept", "title": "Cartesian skepticism"}, {"id": "e3c0d7c9-befb-45fe-b514-5ac50e919d22", "type": "concept", "title": "evil demon"}, {"id": "9e77d12c-4981-4085-92b0-710a088f6c94", "type": "concept", "title": "brain in a vat"}, {"id": "3b37a443-5fab-4f2f-b86c-16ace0c7eee9", "type": "concept", "title": "dream argument"}, {"id": "396fb997-36e7-4d84-bb04-77e4c9634c81", "type": "concept", "title": "external world"}, {"id": "6d10afe0-9c00-4215-858a-4bb76167209b", "type": "concept", "title": "closure principle"}, {"id": "e22ee862-fbc2-40dd-a0d5-dc3f3bca1ac7", "type": "concept", "title": "fallibilism"}, {"id": "e14e6c7f-42ae-49bd-bc25-dfa657d0cdef", "type": "concept", "title": "certainty"}, {"id": "4f91dbff-45c5-4f81-be01-aff6cbd5df16", "type": "concept", "title": "common sense realism"}], "description": "Students learn how radical doubt pressures ordinary claims to knowledge."}, {"id": "c84017a9-16bf-4b13-83ae-854f88deb0de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence, testimony, and epistemic responsibility", "children": [{"id": "fd26a7cf-fd89-4a24-acc6-7b466234e633", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"